WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.780
This video is sponsored by Bokksu.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:07.819
No other character represents the moral landscape
of the one piece world as well as Monkey D.

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:10.610
Garp, the hero of the marines.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.710
As the father of the most wanted person in
the world as well as the grandfather of the

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:19.589
future pirate king and the son of the old
one, garp without any doubt plays a quite

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:24.409
unique role in the story, especially given
the fact that he is one of the most respected

00:00:24.409 --> 00:00:36.140
members within the marines, the sworn enemy
of pirates and revolutionaries alike.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.210
And yet, the two defining traits of his character,
next to his kindhearted and goofy nature are

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.269
his strong sense of duty as well as his love
for his criminal family.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:50.920
And as we will see, it is exactly this stark
polarization of beliefs that make him such

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.379
a tragic and lovable person.

00:00:53.379 --> 00:01:08.890
This is the story of Monkey D. Garp.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:14.229
Garp is mostly known for two feats, the defeat
of the rocks pirates on god valley, as well

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:15.799
as the capture of gol d.

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:16.820
Roger.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.909
Even tough garp has enjoyed immense respect
and special treatment within the marines for

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:24.030
them, both of these events have been doctored.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:29.909
As we now know, Roger actually handed himself
in willingly to trigger the next pirate era.

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.600
Meanwhile, he actually fought side by side
with garp to defeat rocks, which makes it

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:44.719
very hard to assess how strong he truly is.

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.479
since he was able to fight with some of the
most powerful beings in the one piece world

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:54.590
however and was offered the position of admiral
multiple times, it is pretty safe to assume

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.840
that garp is very much the real deal.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.590
From a storytelling perspective, garp actually
has a quite unique character design.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:08.580
Or, to put it in better terms, he doesn't
seem to fit in any traditional trope or category.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.720
Even though he is the grandfather to both
luffy and ace, and was the one who trained

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.250
them both, he doesn't really fit the trope
of the classical old man mentor.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:23.280
That role falls to Rayleigh for luffy and
to whitebeard for ace. a better fit might

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.090
be that of a parental figure, that he Cleary
is to both of the boys.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.700
However while he showered both of them with
love, he also didn't exactly stick around

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.840
all too much.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.890
in the end, I believe that garp is several
important supporting characters mashed into

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.320
one.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.120
he represents the old era from the marines
perspective, that includes other legends,

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:53.700
like Roger or whitebeard.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.650
He is a father figure to the main character,
balanced in such a way that luffy has experienced

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:04.870
both love and care in his childhood, while
still benefitting from the classical shone-hero-without-parents

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.800
trope, that gives him independence and drive.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.951
Kind of ironic actually that luffy mostly
grew up an orphan, even though he has an actual

00:03:12.951 --> 00:03:16.410
father and grandfather who are both still
alive and well.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:21.030
The biggest role garp plays in the story however,
is that he represents the blurred moral lines

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:25.510
between the different groups operating in
the one piece world like no other.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.790
as we all know, the notion that all marines
are good and all pirates are evil is pretty

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.580
much thrown out the window within the first
few chapters.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.260
instead, we learn that there are good marines
and bad marines, just as there are good pirates

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.560
and bad pirates.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.870
And of course a ton of people who fall somewhere
in between.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:48.230
We know that the marines, while claiming to
fight for peace and justice, also serve at

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.700
the will of the celestial dragons, a tyrannical
regime of hedonic slave owners.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.910
At the same time, while a lot of pirates simply
seek freedom from this regime of oppression,

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:02.380
many are just as terrible on the other end
of the table, killing and terrorizing the

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:06.590
innocent civilians who are helplessly caught
between both fronts.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:12.710
And Monkey D. Garp is the personification
of the question: What does it mean to be good.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:16.540
This is actually a really interesting theme
in the monkey family.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:22.889
While luffy values family above all else,
as we see with his crew and ace, and rejects

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:30.000
any sense of duty to any system, his father
Dragon ended up putting duty above all else,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.050
even if it meant abandoning his own child.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:38.930
Garp meanwhile is literally torn between both
duty and family, looking for a way to balance

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.659
them, not always successfully.

00:04:41.659 --> 00:04:46.301
In the end, what all three of them desire
in the end is freedom and a just world, free

00:04:46.301 --> 00:04:54.639
of the terror of the celestial dragons, but
also from pirates like Blackbeard or doflamingo.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:05:02.919
However, based on each of their ideals, Luffy
chose the path of piracy, dragon that of the

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:05.999
revolutionary and garp that of the marine.

00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:11.150
And while luffy represents the best within
the world of pirates, garp very clearly embodies

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:13.159
the best within the marines.

00:05:13.159 --> 00:05:17.639
His approach to justice - I have actually
talked about that off the 4 admirals as well

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:23.919
- are by far the most human and relatable,
making him the flagship of the type of marines,

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:28.500
that we as an audience want to see, and that
inn the future will likely end up becoming

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.500
the new normal.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:38.400
This includes people like smoker or Aokiji,
who see him as a role model, but also a line

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:47.900
of young marines like Coby, who garp chose
and trained himself.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:51.880
I would argue then that garp, as a member
of the d.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:58.050
Clan and the notorious monkey family is the
one who is quietly nursing a more just and

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:03.449
independent generation of marines, with the
freedom and desire to actually work for and

00:06:03.449 --> 00:06:07.849
protect the people and not the celestial dragons.

